  "term": "Embedded Figures Test",
  "definition": "The Embedded Figures Test is a measure used to study field dependence and field independence, a cognitive-style dimension involving how people perceive and solve problems. In this context, higher scores are linked with stronger local processing, meaning better identification of features within a larger whole.",
